#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186347142 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ed5facf-f654-5890-974f-bbdcd9641515" :knowledge-point/title "Applying De Moivre's Theorem to Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf8ef90e-855a-51db-b04e-3ae4203c7f1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5\\theta }{3})-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5\\theta }{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347144} {:answer/id #uuid "13eec265-fa1a-527b-8899-58b5980cdf1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\theta }{5})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\theta }{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347145} {:answer/id #uuid "6c56a2b4-7289-5889-aed5-525ee8a4036a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15[\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347146} {:answer/id #uuid "b2e89d45-82a6-5a2a-a846-f34f4193f309" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(15\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(15\\theta )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347147} {:answer/id #uuid "b850ec25-4f57-59d7-8804-62441bd734d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\theta )]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347148}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b2e89d45-82a6-5a2a-a846-f34f4193f309" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(15\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(15\\theta )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347147} :answer-field/id #uuid "fca9c05d-d7e3-545e-a5d1-3545089ebb79" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347143}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5fe46279-8589-565d-a925-837c7d9f7807" :question/math-academy-id "q-104123" :question/problem "Simplify the expression $\\frac{1}{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡5\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡5\\theta ]^{3}}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡5\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡5\\theta ]^{3}}=[\\operatorname{cos}⁡5\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡5\\theta ]^{-3}.\n$$\n\nDe Moivre's Theorem states that\n\n$$\n[\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\phi +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\phi ]^{n}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\phi )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\phi ).\n$$\n\nIn our expression, we have $n=-3$ and $\\phi =5\\theta .$ Substituting in these values, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡5\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡5\\theta ]^{3}} & =[\\operatorname{cos}⁡5\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡5\\theta ]^{-3} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5(-3)\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5(-3)\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-15\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-15\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the fact that $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\phi )=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\phi )$ and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\phi )=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\phi )$ for any input $\\phi ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-15\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-15\\theta )=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(15\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(15\\theta ).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186347149 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cbc91582-8d44-5de1-9c98-1c5de173eefb" :knowledge-point/title "Applying De Moivre's Theorem With a Negative Sine"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0733eb2f-c336-5451-846e-2318e4be2758" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8\\theta )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347151} {:answer/id #uuid "0fcfe884-a41c-532c-a895-2a4339814644" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2})]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347152} {:answer/id #uuid "b56b4c2f-f5e9-5076-a687-9ad14e3609d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2})-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2})]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347153} {:answer/id #uuid "67a91845-b458-5f57-bd5c-9b817a584ad0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8\\theta )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347154} {:answer/id #uuid "19acf000-98cf-52d0-8c89-e20241a47b48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(16\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(16\\theta )]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347155}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "67a91845-b458-5f57-bd5c-9b817a584ad0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8\\theta )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347154} :answer-field/id #uuid "46e68718-763a-535b-af30-97f696256d1f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347150}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a7fb8fd7-85f4-5c55-8097-022bd414615d" :question/math-academy-id "q-17330" :question/problem "Simplify the expression ${[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2})-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2})]}^{16}.$" :question/worked-solution "For expressions involving subtraction, De Moivre's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\phi )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\phi )]}^{n}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\phi )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\phi ).\n$$\n\nIn our expression, we have $n=16$ and $\\phi =\\frac{\\theta }{2}.$ Substituting in these values, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2})-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2})]}^{16} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(16\\cdot \\frac{\\theta }{2})-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(16\\cdot \\frac{\\theta }{2}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186347156 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ed5facf-f654-5890-974f-bbdcd9641515" :knowledge-point/title "Applying De Moivre's Theorem to Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8f2b50f4-ac77-5ed5-852c-67a6fd4947ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cos(10\\theta)-i\\sin(10\\theta)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347158} {:answer/id #uuid "2e4f56e1-c178-59ae-8aa7-eb7803b760f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cos(10\\theta)+i\\sin(10\\theta)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347159}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8f2b50f4-ac77-5ed5-852c-67a6fd4947ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cos(10\\theta)-i\\sin(10\\theta)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347158} :answer-field/id #uuid "06cf9771-cdad-50c9-a09f-15a38efc2cb3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347157}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3c28e84b-c53e-504e-b8c2-0b7814a2c45f" :question/math-academy-id "q-325322" :question/problem "Simplify the expression $\\frac{1}{{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )]}^{10}}.$ Use $i$ to denote the imaginary unit.\n\n$\\frac{1}{{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )]}^{10}}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, note that\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )]}^{10}}={[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )]}^{-10}.\n$$\n\nDe Moivre's Theorem states that\n\n$$\n{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\phi )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\phi )]}^{n}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\phi )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\phi ).\n$$\n\nIn our expression, we have $n=-10$ and $\\phi =\\theta .$ Substituting in these values, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )]}^{10}} & ={[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )]}^{-10} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-10\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-10\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the fact that $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\phi )=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\phi )$ and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\phi )=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\phi )$ for any input $\\phi ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-10\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-10\\theta )=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(10\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(10\\theta ).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186347160 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ed5facf-f654-5890-974f-bbdcd9641515" :knowledge-point/title "Applying De Moivre's Theorem to Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95a4f400-c75c-5613-aad7-af0f436ee8b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\cos(4\\theta)-3i\\sin(4\\theta)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347162}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "95a4f400-c75c-5613-aad7-af0f436ee8b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\cos(4\\theta)-3i\\sin(4\\theta)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347162} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5aebd88-b9d1-569f-9e98-c0ef454c7959" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347161}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "56395c12-56d9-5b2e-a8bf-03ab5ebc1eb1" :question/math-academy-id "q-325325" :question/problem "Simplify the expression $\\frac{3}{{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )]}^{4}},$ where $x$ and $y$ are functions of $\\theta .$ Use $i$ to denote the imaginary unit.\n\n$\\frac{3}{{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )]}^{4}}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, note that\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )]}^{4}}=3{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )]}^{-4}.\n$$\n\nDe Moivre's Theorem states that\n\n$$\n{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\phi )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\phi )]}^{n}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\phi )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\phi ).\n$$\n\nIn our expression, we have $n=-4$ and $\\phi =\\theta .$ Substituting in these values, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )]}^{4}} & =3{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )]}^{-4} \\\\  & =3[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-4\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-4\\theta )].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the fact that $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\phi )=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\phi )$ and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\phi )=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\phi )$ for any input $\\phi ,$ we have\n\n$$\n3[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-4\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-4\\theta )]=3[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\theta )].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186347163 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cbc91582-8d44-5de1-9c98-1c5de173eefb" :knowledge-point/title "Applying De Moivre's Theorem With a Negative Sine"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "daaaf824-12e2-5927-bdf3-a4bd9af7d26e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\cos(20\\theta)+4i\\sin(20\\theta)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347165}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "daaaf824-12e2-5927-bdf3-a4bd9af7d26e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\cos(20\\theta)+4i\\sin(20\\theta)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347165} :answer-field/id #uuid "d11956c1-8012-5219-8bf3-fd4c5f5f9e84" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347164}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2c1e61a2-b8d6-58ca-b034-10df8d60647c" :question/math-academy-id "q-325346" :question/problem "Express $\\frac{4}{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\theta )]^{5}}$ in the form $x+\\text{i}y,$ where $x$ and $y$ are functions of $\\theta .$ Use $i$ to denote the imaginary unit.\n\n$\\frac{4}{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\theta )]^{5}}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, note that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\theta )]}^{5}} & =4{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\theta )]}^{-5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor expressions involving subtraction, De Moivre's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\phi )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\phi )]}^{n}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\phi )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\phi ).\n$$\n\nIn our expression, we have $n=-5$ and $\\phi =4\\theta .$ Substituting in these values, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\theta )]}^{-5} & =4[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-5\\cdot 4\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-5\\cdot 4\\theta )] \\\\  & =4[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-20\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-20\\theta )].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the fact that $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\phi )=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\phi )$ and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\phi )=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\phi )$ for any input $\\phi ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-20\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-20\\theta )] & =4[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(20\\theta )-[-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(20\\theta )]] \\\\  & =4[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(20\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(20\\theta )].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n4{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\theta )]}^{-5}=4[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(20\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(20\\theta )].\n$$"}]}
